{"id":"word:hebrew:H4428","type":"word","title":"מֶלֶךְ","subtitle":"H4428 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a king","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מֶלֶךְ (H4428) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 2526 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מֶלֶךְ (melek) means a king First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 43."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מֶלֶךְ","transliteration":"melek","pronunciation":"meh'-lek","strong":"H4428","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4428","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מֶֽלֶךְ","מֶ֣לֶךְ","הַ/מֶּ֔לֶךְ","הַ/מֶּ֖לֶךְ","הַ/מֶּֽלֶךְ"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",1045],["HNcmsc",787],["HNcmsa",112],["HNcmpc",110],["HRd/Ncmsa",103],["HR/Ncmsa",42],["HNcmpa",41],["HR/Ncmpc",40],["HTd/Ncmpa",38],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",35]]},"definitions":{"short":"a king","usage":"king, royal.","full":"H4428. melek I. מֶ֫לֶךְ 2513 noun masculine king (Late Hebrew id. ; MI 1, 5, 10, 18, 23 מלך ; Neh 1:4 המלכן ; Phoenician מלך ; Zinjirli מלך DHM Sendsch. 60 ; Assyrian maliku , malku , prince (Assyrian šarru = king ); Arabic king (original Hebrew * מַלִח inferred, Lag BN 73 Ba NB § 112 WMM As. u. Europ.76 ); Sabean מלכן SabDenkm No. 1 ; construct מלך , plural אמלך CIS iv 37 ; compare Ethiopic God (and Nö l.c .); Aramaic , מְלֵיךְ ; Palmyrene מלכא מלך Vog No. 28 ; Nabataean מלכא Eut Nab. 1 ); — ׳מ absolute Gen 14:7 + (insert also 2Sam 13:17 ᵐ5 Th We Dr Kit Bu, and 13:34 ᵐ5 We Dr Kit Bu); in p. always מֶ֑לֶךְ Gen 49:20 238t. (so also proper name in מֶלֶךְ -); construct 14:1 +; suffix מַלְכִּי 2 Samuel 19:44 6 t., etc.; plural מְלָכִים 14:9 +; מְלָכִין Prov 31:3 ; construct מַלְכֵי Gen 17:16 +; suffix מְלָכֶיהָ Isa 7:16 3 t.; מַלְכֵיהֶם Deut 7:24 16 t., etc.; — 1 king: of Egypt Gen 39:20 f.; Exod 1:8 f.; Deut 11:3 ; 1Kin 3:1 ; of Mesopotamia, Shinar, Assyria, Babylon, Persia, etc. Judg 3:8 , 10 ; Gen 14:1 f.; 2Kin 15:19-20 , 29 ; 17:3 f.; 18:13 f.; 24:1 , 11 f.; Ezra 1:1 f.; 4:3 f.; Est 1:2 +, 1Kin 11:18 , 40 ; 14:25 ; 2Kin 17:4 f.; 23:29 +; of Canaan, Philistia, Edom, Moab, etc. (often of single city): Gen 14:2 f.; 14:18 ; 20:2 ; 26:1 , 8 ; 36:31 ; Num 20:14 ; 21:1 f.; 22:4 , 10 ; Deut 1:4 ; 3:1 f.; Josh 2:2 (often in Joshua), Judg 1:7 ; 5:19 ; 8:5 , 12 ; 11:12 f.; 2Kin 3:4 f. +; of Aram, Hamath, etc. 2Sam 8:3 f. 8:9 ; 1Kin 15:18 ; 20:1 f.; 22:3 ; 2Kin 5:1 f.; 8:7 f.; 8:29 ; 9:14-15 , 15:37 ; 16:5 f. +; of Tyre, etc. 2Sam 5:11 ; 1Kin 5:15 ; 9:11 , 16 +, etc.; especially of Israel (undivided, and of both divisions) Gen 36:31 ; Num 23:21 ; 24:7 ; Deut 17:14 f.; Judg 17:6 ; 18:1 ; 19:1 ; 21:25 ; 1Sam 2:10 ; 8:5 f.; 2Sam 2:4 f.; 1Kin 1:33-34 ,f. + very often; compare also Judg 9:5 . &#8212; 2Sam 18:29 b strike out ׳הַמּ We Klo Dr Kit Bu. Note that in early books דוד המלך is nearly always said; in late books usually וגו ׳שׁלמה המלך ) דוד ; compare Aramaic מַלְכָּא כּוֺרֶשׁ , etc. 2 of Davidic king, as under divine protection , 1Sam 2:10 (|| מְשִׁיחוֺ ), Psa 2:6 ; Psalm 18:51; 89:19 ; 61:7 , compare 99:4 ; so in (Messianic) prediction Hosea 3:5 ; Isa 32:1 ; Jer 23:5 ; Ezek 37:22 , 24 ; Zech 9:9 . 3 used of ׳י as king of Israel 1Sam 12:12 ; in poetry Deut 33:5 compare Psa 5:3 ; 10:16 ; 29:10 ; 44:5 ; 48:3 ; 68:25 ; 74:12 ; 84:4 ; 145:1 ; 149:2 ; Isa 41:21 ; 43:15 ; 44:6 ; Zeph 3:15 ; הַכָּבוֺד מֶלֶךְ Psa 24:7 ; 24:8 ; 24:9 ; 24:10 (twice in verse); universal king 47:3 ; 47:8 ; 95:3 ; 98:6 ; Jer 10:7 , 10 , compare 46:18 ; 48:15 ; 51:57 ; Zech 14:9 , 16 , 17 ; Mal 1:14 ; of false god Amos 5:26 . 4 in fable, king of trees Judg 9:8 , 15 figurative of crocodile Job 41:26 ; ׳מ לָאַרְבֶּה אֵין Prov 30:27 ; of death, בַּלָּהוֺת מֶלֶךְ Job 18:14 . 5 combinations are: — a. ׳הַמּ הַגָּדוֺל 2Kin 18:19 , 28 = Isa 36:4 , 13 (of Assyrian king: compare Assyrian šarru rabu ); ׳מ גָּדוֺל Eccl 9:14 (indefinite); of ׳י Mal 1:14 , ׳מ ׳ג עַלכֿלאֿלהים Psa 95:3 ; עוֺלָם ׳מ Jer 10:10 (of ׳י ); ׳מ מְלָכִים Ezek 26:7 (king of Babylon) b. הַמֶּלֶךְ יְחִי 1Sam 10:24 ; 2Sam 16:16 (twice in verse); 1Kin 1:34 , 39 ; 2Kin 11:12 ; 2Chr 23:11 ; בירושׁלם מֶלֶךְ Eccl 1:1 , compare Eccl 15:26; 2Sam 5:2 ; 1Kin 14:2 ; 1Chr 29:25 ; 2Sam 2:11 ( מ עלהֿיה ׳בחברון ) 1Kin 11:37 ; 2Chr 28:4 ; Eccl 1:12 . c. following a verb (one or two accusative) מ ׳שִׂים על Deut 17:14-15 , (twice in verse); 1Sam 10:19 ; מ לָנוּ ׳שִׂים 8:5 ; לְמ ׳שִׂים 1Kin 10:9 ; מ ׳נָתַן לְ 1Sam 8:6 ; Hosea 13:10-11 , עַל נָתַן 1Sam 12:13 ; 2Chr 2:10 ; Neh 9:37 ; 13:26 ; לְמֶלֶךְ הִמְלִיךְ Judg 9:6 ; 1Sam 15:11 ; מ ׳הִמְלִיךְ על 12:1 ; מ ׳הִמְלִיךְ לְ 8:22 ; עַל מ ׳מָשַׁח Judg 9:8 ; לְמ ׳מָשַׁח 1Kin 1:45 ; לְמ ׳מָשַׁךְ עַל Judg 9:15 ; 1Sam 15:1 , 17 ; 2Sam 2:4 ; 5:3 , 12 ; 12:7 ; 1Kin 1:34 ; 1Chr 11:3 ; 14:8 ; ׳מ על יִהְיֶה 1Sam 8:19 ; למ ׳בִּקֵּשׁ על 2Sam 3:17 ; על לְמ ׳הֵכִין 5:12 ; 1Chr 14:2 ; מ ׳הֵקִים על 1Kin 14:14 ; Deut 28:36 ; י עַלכִּֿסֵּא ׳יָשַׁב ׳לְמ וגו ׳תַּחַת 1Chr 29:23 , compare Prov 20:8 ; לְמ עַלכִּֿסֵּא ׳נָתַן ׳לְי אלהיך 2Chr 9:8 . d. מַעֲדַנֵּימֶֿלךְ Gen 49:20 royal dainties , figurative; הַמּ ׳מִשְׁתֵּה 1Sam 25:36 royal feast (in simile); הַמּ ׳אֶבֶן 2Sam 14:26 king's weight ; ׳יַדהַֿמּ 1Kin 10:13 royal bounty (in simile); הַמּ ׳גִּזֵּי Amos 7:1 king's mowings ; מ ׳מִקְדַּשׁ 7:13 royal sanctuary ; מַלְכָּם עֲטֶרֶת 2Sam 12:30 crown of their king = 1Chr 20:2 (but read ᵐ5 מִלְכֹּם We Klo Dr Kit Kau — not Bu Kit Chr. Hpt); compare also שָׁוֵה גַּן, עֵמֶק, בַּיִת, , etc. — proper name עבד מלך, נתן, מלך, אלימלך, אחימלך, אבימלך, , see below אח אב, , etc. מַלְכִישׁוּעַ proper name, masculine son of Saul my king (= ׳י ) is opulence , compare Gray Prop. N. 147 ); — 1Sam 14:49 ; 31:2 ; 1Chr 8:33 ; 9:39 ; 10:2 (in Chronicles מַלְכִּישֿׁוּעַ ). ᵐ5 Μελχεισα , Μελχεσουε , etc.","rootNote":"from 4427 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 43","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 43","1Chr 1 43","1Chr 3 2","1Chr 4 23","1Chr 4 41","1Chr 5 6","1Chr 5 17","1Chr 5 17"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":